gomodel:6ab067da00014629
        a                      owl:Ontology ;
        rdfs:comment           "Downstream arm added 2026-11-11: cAMP -> PRKACA (cAMP-dependent protein kinase) -> SUR2B (ABCC9 isoform O60706-2, potassium channel regulator activity) -> Kir6.1 (KCNJ8) K_ATP channel, K+ efflux, hyperpolarization and relaxation of vascular smooth muscle. CGRP -> PKA -> K_ATP currents shown in rabbit mesenteric (PMID:8189394) and pig coronary (PMID:9490826) arterial myocytes; human placental vessel relaxation to CGRP blocked by Rp-cAMPS and glibenclamide (PMID:14684361); human iPSC-VSMC K_ATP currents (PMID:38984978). Direct PKA phosphorylation of SUR2B Ser1387 activating Kir6.1/SUR2B shown with rat Kir6.1 + mouse SUR2B clones (PMID:17596331, PMID:18198173; also PMID:15087422), so those edges are ISS (GO_REF:0000024) from MGI:MGI:1352630 / RGD:2960. Alternative Gbetagamma -> Kv7/BKCa route (human coronary, PMID:38583945; rat, PMID:42157312) not modelled." , "Built 2026-11-11 from skeleton gomodel:66a3e0bb00001742 (CALCB -> CALCRL-RAMP1 -> GNAS -> ADCY6 -> cAMP), recast in the target cell: vascular associated smooth muscle cell (CL:0000359), with the CGRP receptor signaling pathway part of relaxation of vascular associated smooth muscle (GO:0060087, is_a vasodilation). Receptor revised 2026-11-12 by the curator: CALCRL enables CGRP receptor activity (CALCB has input CALCRL; CALCRL has input and directly activates GNAS), and RAMP1 coreceptor activity directly positively regulates CALCRL (PMID:33602864, PMID:30209400)." , "Evidence caveat: human beta-CGRP relaxes human arteries endothelium-independently (PMID:14642788, PMID:3495374, PMID:15983761), but the cAMP dependence of CGRP vasorelaxation varies by vascular bed: AC/PKA inhibitors reduce it in human thymic arteries (PMID:12529288), whereas in human coronary arteries it is AC/PKA-independent and Gbetagamma-dependent (PMID:38583945). The AC isoform in vascular smooth muscle downstream of the CGRP receptor is not established; ADCY6 is kept from the skeleton. Downstream effectors of cAMP (PKA, K+ channels) are deliberately not modelled. Several references were evaluated from abstracts only (no PMC full text): 14642788, 3495374, 11804624, 12529288, 17916776, 17110384, 12135370, 1318039." , "Curated with GO AI HUB. Beta-CGRP (CALCB) signaling via the CALCRL-RAMP1 CGRP receptor, Gs, adenylate cyclase, cAMP, PKA and the SUR2B/Kir6.1 KATP channel in relaxation of vascular smooth muscle (Human)." ;
        lego:conforms_to_gpad  false ;
        lego:modelstate        "production" ;
        dc:contributor         "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7646-0052" ;
        dc:date                "2026-11-24" ;
        dc:title               "Vascular smooth muscle relaxation by CALCB/beta-CGRP (Human)" ;
        pav:providedBy         "https://www.uniprot.org" , "http://geneontology.org" ;
        owl:versionIRI         gomodel:6ab067da00014629 ;
        biolink:in_taxon       obo:NCBITaxon_9606 .

